-- Robscript Team - Throw Food For Baddies
-- Game: Throw Food For Baddies | placeId 89727004942007 | gameId 10773616048
-- Window: RightControl | Unload: Settings -> Unload | API: getgenv().RobScriptTFFB
--
-- What it does:
--   One switch. "Auto farm" runs the whole chain: throw with the power meter pinned to the top,
--   put the caught baddie into the pen, keep the best baddies in the pen, sell the leftovers,
--   buy the best fruit you can afford, upgrade the pen and the pull-up bar.
--   Rotation adds bar phases on a timer, where the same chain keeps the pen tidy and trains
--   Throwing Strength.
--
-- How it works: the game is fully remote driven and every remote is reachable from the client.
--   Throw.Begin(false) opens a throw session and returns the server MeterStart. The power meter is
--   a triangle wave (MeterAt in ThrowConfig, period 1.6 s, peak 0.8 s after MeterStart) and the
--   server computes the meter from the timestamp sent in Throw.Tap, so tapping exactly on the peak
--   gives meter ~0.99 and max power. The game's own auto throw asks the server for a random low
--   AutoMeter, that is why it feels weak.
--   A caught baddie becomes a HeldBaddie tool; Pen.Place(Vector3) drops it into the pen, so the
--   script only has to hand over a point inside your own pen. Pen.EquipBest, Pen.Unequip,
--   FoodShop.Buy/Equip, Upgrade.PenPress, PullUp.Start/Stop and the Sell stall check the distance
--   server side, so the script teleports to the matching station, does the action and comes back.
--   Sell.Sell takes an array of baddie uids and needs you to stand at the hub Sell stall.

do
	local existing = getgenv().RobScriptTFFB
	if type(existing) == "table" and type(existing.Destroy) == "function" then
